## Why This Matters

**Scripts ARE the Game**

The C++ server is just:
- Network protocol (connect clients)
- Database (store characters)
- Physics (movement, combat)

The **game** is in Lua:
- When monsters spawn (ambush system)
- Where treasure appears (chest system)
- How NPCs behave (traveler system)

If Lua doesn't run, there's no game.

**Silent Failure is Deadly**

The worst kind of bug:
- No error messages
- Server appears to work
- Game just... doesn't happen

Hours of debugging: "Why aren't monsters spawning?!"
Answer: "Lua engine never initialized."

**One Hook Change**

The fix was 15 lines of C++. But finding it took:
- Grep through AC codebase
- Test multiple hooks
- Understand module loading
- Read playerbots source (working example)
- Trial and error

That's why this issue exists. Document the discovery.

